# The matrix cases that disagree with the pinned SQLite 3.53.4 because of a
# defect that is not fixed yet.
#
# One per line: the case id, a tab, the bug's number in the description of
# task-2136 ("Inillucent Test Suite Bugs Found"), a tab, and one sentence.
#
# A listed case that still disagrees passes. A listed case that now agrees at
# every arm it ran at fails, with a message saying to take its line off: a fix
# cannot land without this list shrinking. A listed id that no case has fails
# `matrix::lists`. Differences that are not defects are rules in
# deliberate.toml, not lines here.
#
# A defect that shows only at some arms writes them after the number:
# `65@small-pool,sqlite-page`. The line is then stale only when the case agrees
# at one of those arms, so a cadence that runs the case only at the default arm
# does not call it fixed.

probe-temp.as.select	8	changes() after CREATE TEMP TABLE AS SELECT counts the copied rows where SQLite leaves it alone.
syntax-alter-table-stmt-p5	12	ALTER TABLE DROP COLUMN succeeds while a view uses the column; SQLite refuses it.
syntax-alter-table-stmt-p6	12	ALTER TABLE DROP (without COLUMN) succeeds while a view uses the column; SQLite refuses it.
probe-prag.maintenance	15	PRAGMA optimize reports no result column where SQLite reports one named optimize.
temp-schema-names	16	sqlite_temp_schema is "no such table" on a connection that has made no TEMP object.
probe-temp.not.main	16	sqlite_temp_schema is "no such table" on a connection that has made no TEMP object.
probe-prag.autovacuum	17	PRAGMA auto_vacuum set on a new file reads back 0 after a reopen where SQLite keeps the setting.
probe-prag.schema.switches	18	PRAGMA writable_schema reads back 0 after it is set on; SQLite reads back 1.

# Generated cases, grouped by bug. Written from the triage of an inillucent-matrix run;
# each line's case fails in the way its bug's section on task-2136 describes.
constraint-f18eefd57be9	1	COMMIT or ROLLBACK with no transaction fails with result code 21 where SQLite gives 1.
